<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barbados</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barbados is an island nation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a>, the southernmost and easternmost island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> region. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a> people lived there from the 13th century, but the indigenous population had mostly been sold into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, killed or died of disease by the time an English ship arrived on 14 May 1625. It became an English and later British colony with a plantation economy that used Irish indentured servants and then enslaved Africans. Barbados became independent on 30 November 1966 and a republic within the Commonwealth on 30 November 2021.</p></div>
